{
  "id": "m03-gcd-lcm-cap",
  "title": "GCD and Capped LCM",
  "source": {
    "name": "Original exercise on Euclid's algorithm and overflow-safe LCM"
  },
  "rating": 1000,
  "tags": [
    "math",
    "gcd",
    "number-theory"
  ],
  "statement": "For each of `t` pairs of positive integers `a` and `b`, print `gcd(a, b)` and `lcm(a, b)`.\n\nThe true LCM can be as large as about `10^36`, so we only ask for it when it is small enough: if `lcm(a, b) > 10^18`, print `-1` in its place.\n\n**Input.** First line: `t`. Then `t` lines, each holding `a` and `b`.\n\n**Output.** `t` lines, each of the form `gcd lcm` (or `gcd -1`).",
  "constraints": [
    "1 ≤ t ≤ 300",
    "1 ≤ a, b ≤ 10^18"
  ],
  "timeLimitMs": 2000,
  "hints": [
    "gcd(a, b) = gcd(b, a mod b) until the second argument is 0. That takes about 90 steps at most for 64-bit values.",
    "lcm(a, b) = a / gcd * b. Computing a * b first can overflow 64-bit integers, so divide before multiplying.",
    "To test lcm > 10^18 without overflowing, let x = a / g and check whether x > 10^18 / b (integer division). If so, the product exceeds the limit. In JavaScript use BigInt."
  ],
  "editorial": "Euclid's algorithm finds the gcd in `O(log min(a, b))` steps. For the LCM use `a / g * b` with the division first: the quotient is exact, and the product `x * b` is at most the final answer.\n\nTo detect `x * b > 10^18` safely in a 64-bit type, compare `x` with `floor(10^18 / b)`: `x * b <= 10^18` exactly when `x <= floor(10^18 / b)`. The tests include pairs on both sides of the boundary, such as `lcm(10^9, 10^9 - 1)` (just under the limit) and `lcm(10^9 + 1, 10^9)` (just over).",
  "complexity": {
    "time": "O(n log n)",
    "space": "O(1)"
  },
  "starter": {
    "python": "import sys\nLIM = 10**18\ndata = sys.stdin.read().split()\nt = int(data[0])\n# for each pair print: gcd, then lcm (or -1 if lcm > LIM)\n",
    "javascript": "// Use BigInt for 10^18-sized values.\nconst t = Number(readLine());\nconst LIM = 10n ** 18n;\n// each next line holds a and b\n",
    "cpp": "#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nint main() {\n    int t;\n    cin >> t;\n    const long long LIM = 1000000000000000000LL;\n    // never compute a * b directly\n}\n",
    "java": "import java.util.*;\nimport java.io.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        StringTokenizer st = new StringTokenizer(new String(System.in.readAllBytes()));\n        int t = Integer.parseInt(st.nextToken());\n        final long LIM = 1_000_000_000_000_000_000L;\n        // never compute a * b directly\n    }\n}\n"
  },
  "solutions": {
    "python": "import sys\nLIM = 10**18\ndata = sys.stdin.read().split()\nt = int(data[0])\nout = []\nfor i in range(t):\n    a = int(data[1 + 2 * i])\n    b = int(data[2 + 2 * i])\n    x, y = a, b\n    while y:\n        x, y = y, x % y\n    g = x\n    l = a // g * b\n    out.append(str(g) + ' ' + str(l if l <= LIM else -1))\nprint('\\n'.join(out))\n",
    "javascript": "const tok = [];\nlet line;\nwhile ((line = readLine()) !== null) for (const t of line.split(/\\s+/)) if (t) tok.push(t);\nlet pos = 0;\nconst t = Number(tok[pos++]);\nconst LIM = 10n ** 18n;\nconst out = [];\nfor (let i = 0; i < t; i++) {\n  const a = BigInt(tok[pos++]);\n  const b = BigInt(tok[pos++]);\n  let x = a, y = b;\n  while (y) { [x, y] = [y, x % y]; }\n  const l = (a / x) * b;\n  out.push(x + ' ' + (l <= LIM ? l : -1n));\n}\nconsole.log(out.join('\\n'));\n",
    "cpp": "#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nint main() {\n    int t;\n    cin >> t;\n    const long long LIM = 1000000000000000000LL;\n    while (t--) {\n        long long a, b;\n        cin >> a >> b;\n        long long x = a, y = b;\n        while (y) { long long r = x % y; x = y; y = r; }\n        long long q = a / x;\n        if (q > LIM / b) cout << x << \" -1\\n\";\n        else cout << x << \" \" << q * b << \"\\n\";\n    }\n}\n",
    "java": "import java.util.*;\nimport java.io.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        StringTokenizer st = new StringTokenizer(new String(System.in.readAllBytes()));\n        int t = Integer.parseInt(st.nextToken());\n        final long LIM = 1_000_000_000_000_000_000L;\n        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();\n        while (t-- > 0) {\n            long a = Long.parseLong(st.nextToken());\n            long b = Long.parseLong(st.nextToken());\n            long x = a, y = b;\n            while (y != 0) { long r = x % y; x = y; y = r; }\n            long q = a / x;\n            if (q > LIM / b) sb.append(x).append(\" -1\\n\");\n            else sb.append(x).append(' ').append(q * b).append('\\n');\n        }\n        System.out.print(sb);\n    }\n}\n"
  },
